\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Precious redeemer, we thank you
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 We have been saved out of your death
\par For the high value of your blood
\par made God pronounce man innocent
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Pardon us Jesus Son of God
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Let your wounds heal us from our sins.
\par Heal O, heal our sinful nature,
\par so we shall have peace in our hearts.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Protect us and take care of us
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 so we are not conquered by sin
\par and whene'er we are in danger
\par Let us then learn to be patient.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Let us give focus on your cross
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 and to comfort our selves always
\par Leave us not, rather follow us
\par \pard        and lead us into your glory.         \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

